Section C: End-to-End Manual Testing Project – Food Delivery Web Portal

Project Name: FoodieExpress
 1. Test Plan
1.1 Project Overview

FoodieExpress is an online food delivery web portal where users can register, log in, search for restaurants, view food items, 
add items to the cart, place orders, and track their orders.

 1.2 Testing Objectives

- Verify that users can register and log in successfully.
- Verify that users can search for restaurants and food items.
- Verify that users can add and remove food items from the cart.
- Verify that users can place orders successfully.
- Verify that payment and order confirmation work correctly.
- Verify that order details are stored correctly in the database.

1.3 Scope of Testing

In Scope:

- User Registration
- User Login and Logout
- Restaurant Search
- Food Item Selection
- Add to Cart and Remove from Cart
- Apply Coupon
- Checkout
- Payment
- Order Confirmation
- Order History and Tracking

Out of Scope:

- Restaurant owner account management
- Delivery partner location tracking system
- Third-party payment gateway internal testing
- Server infrastructure testing

 1.4 Testing Approach

- Manual Testing
- Functional Testing
- UI Testing
- Integration Testing
- End-to-End Testing
- Negative Testing
- Database Testing
- Regression Testing

1.5 Test Environment

- Operating System: Windows 10/11
- Browser: Google Chrome
- Testing Type: Manual Testing
- Database: MySQL
- Application: FoodieExpress Web Portal

1.6 Entry Criteria

- Application build should be available.
- Requirements should be clearly defined.
- Test environment should be ready.
- Required test data should be available.

 1.7 Exit Criteria

- All planned test cases should be executed.
- Critical and high-severity defects should be fixed and retested.
- Test execution results should be documented.
- Testing summary report should be prepared.

1.8 Risks and Mitigation

Risk 1: Application may not be available.
- Mitigation: Check the testing environment before starting execution.

Risk 2: Invalid or incomplete test data.
- Mitigation: Prepare valid and invalid test data before testing.

Risk 3: Payment gateway failure.
- Mitigation: Use a payment sandbox or test payment environment.


